WEBVTT

00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:04.894
This is an overview of tvx, a free charting terminal for Binance and Bybit.

00:00:04.944 --> 00:00:16.220
We will go from simple to advanced: the first launch and the chart, windows, the screener and watchlists, drawing and positions, and finally quick tricks, sync and the phone.

00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:19.071
Part 1. First launch.

00:00:19.879 --> 00:00:23.557
On the first launch the terminal asks for a couple of settings.

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:26.220
The interface language is English or Russian.

00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:30.650
The theme is light, dark or the system one.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:38.526
Then the time zone for intraday charts, and the exchange and market where coins open.

00:00:39.036 --> 00:00:42.240
All of this can be changed later in the settings.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.170
Press “Start”.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.750
Here are three windows of one coin: five minutes at the top, the daily chart bottom left and the hourly one on the right.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.353
On the right is the panel with the screener, watchlists, checklist and alerts.

00:00:55.862 --> 00:01:00.007
To change the coin, just start typing its name and the search opens.

00:01:00.057 --> 00:01:03.523
Press Enter, and the coin changes in all windows at once.

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:07.991
The interval of the active window is switched with the buttons at the top.

00:01:08.041 --> 00:01:11.787
The drop-down has all intervals, and the star puts one on the toolbar.

00:01:12.288 --> 00:01:15.815
You can also type the interval: digits mean minutes.

00:01:15.865 --> 00:01:19.255
Type 15 and Enter, and 5 brings back five minutes.

00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:22.637
Part 2. The chart and its look.

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:29.430
Drag the chart with the mouse in any direction, and the wheel zooms the time scale.

00:01:29.925 --> 00:01:35.544
The wheel over the price scale stretches the chart vertically, and the “auto” button resets the scale.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:38.379
Another coin opens with the same zoom and position.

00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:44.382
Next to the last price is the time until the candle closes, and the price is colored like the bar.

00:01:44.432 --> 00:01:47.160
The grid and time scale continue into the future.

00:01:47.654 --> 00:01:56.013
The chart type menu has bars, candles, hollow candles, Heikin Ashi and line, plus thin bars and the current price line.

00:01:56.513 --> 00:02:01.016
The time zone is changed with the button in the bottom right corner of the chart.

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:04.894
Intraday charts show the chosen time, daily ones show exchange dates.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:17.237
The gear menu has the theme, custom colors and the “Fonts, timer, position size” window: larger scale and legend fonts, the candle timer and the deposit used for position size.

00:02:17.753 --> 00:02:21.692
Alt+Enter maximizes the active window and restores the layout.

00:02:21.742 --> 00:02:28.511
Alt+G jumps all windows to a date, and the arrow at the bottom right brings you back to the current price.

00:02:28.961 --> 00:02:31.797
Part 3. Windows and templates.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:37.185
Pick the layout here: up to eight charts, presets or your own grid.

00:02:37.235 --> 00:02:41.257
Below is window sync: symbol, interval, crosshair and time.

00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:47.579
The crosshair is mirrored in every window, which helps to compare one spot on different intervals.

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:50.271
Window and side panel borders can be dragged.

00:02:50.777 --> 00:02:55.626
Save a good setup as a template: layout, intervals, chart types and indicators.

00:02:55.676 --> 00:03:01.703
A starred template becomes a toolbar button, and it can be bound to the Screener or Watchlist tab.

00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:04.553
Part 4. Screener.

00:03:05.378 --> 00:03:13.667
The Screener tab lists the exchange coins that match your conditions: exchange, market, daily turnover, price change and sorting.

00:03:13.717 --> 00:03:18.128
You can also show only crypto, only stocks and TradFi, or everything.

00:03:18.619 --> 00:03:21.833
Columns are configurable: price, change, volume.

00:03:21.883 --> 00:03:26.592
The price is colored by the daily change, and clicking a header sorts.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.964
Clicking a row opens the coin.

00:03:29.014 --> 00:03:35.376
Space pages through the screener, Shift+Space goes back, and the arrow keys move one coin at a time.

00:03:35.876 --> 00:03:40.997
Left of the name is the direction mark: one click marks the coin long, a second one short.

00:03:41.047 --> 00:03:45.650
The dot on the right shows which lists the coin is in and adds it to any of them.

00:03:46.148 --> 00:03:52.032
You can take several coins at once: Ctrl+click picks them one by one, Shift+click picks a range.

00:03:52.082 --> 00:03:56.545
Right-click, and all of them get a direction and go to the list you need.

00:03:56.995 --> 00:03:59.423
Part 5. Watchlists.

00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:03.418
On the Watchlist tab all your lists flow as sections.

00:04:03.468 --> 00:04:06.914
Each has a color tag, and clicking the name collapses it.

00:04:06.964 --> 00:04:08.815
Prices and changes update live.

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:13.715
The star marks the current list: coins go there with Alt+W and on paste.

00:04:13.765 --> 00:04:18.847
Coins and whole lists are dragged with the mouse, or with a long press on a tablet.

00:04:19.345 --> 00:04:22.172
The switch at the top filters by direction.

00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:27.792
Next to it: share the list, paste coins from the clipboard, columns, and a new list.

00:04:28.288 --> 00:04:36.790
“Share list” makes, for every checked coin, a picture with all windows and a line “coin, direction, level”, handy to send to Telegram.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.640
Part 6. Drawing.

00:04:41.703 --> 00:04:43.716
Drawing tools are on the left.

00:04:43.766 --> 00:04:47.497
A horizontal level takes one click, fastest with Alt+H.

00:04:47.547 --> 00:04:50.660
The level price shows right away on the scale.

00:04:51.155 --> 00:04:55.689
The level belongs to the coin, not the window, so it shows on every interval.

00:04:55.739 --> 00:04:59.440
Handles appear on hover, and you can drag a drawing right away.

00:04:59.937 --> 00:05:04.136
Click the line to open its panel: color, width, style, label.

00:05:04.186 --> 00:05:08.942
Drag the panel by its grip wherever you like, even outside the chart.

00:05:09.456 --> 00:05:16.268
Timeframe visibility works like in TradingView: tick any intervals one by one, as groups, or with a preset.

00:05:16.318 --> 00:05:20.309
For example, keep this level only on five minutes and one hour.

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:23.466
Trend lines and rectangles take two clicks.

00:05:23.516 --> 00:05:29.923
The magnet snaps points to candle prices: it has three modes, and the crosshair can snap to prices too.

00:05:30.426 --> 00:05:33.323
The Text tool: click on the chart and type.

00:05:33.373 --> 00:05:38.051
Text has size, color and background, and can be pinned to the screen.

00:05:38.557 --> 00:05:41.965
Ctrl+Z undoes, Delete removes the selected drawing.

00:05:42.015 --> 00:05:46.100
Arrow keys nudge a drawing, and dragging with Ctrl copies it.

00:05:46.594 --> 00:05:51.368
The pencil, Alt+B, draws freehand: circle an area or sketch an arrow.

00:05:51.418 --> 00:05:57.731
It stays active until you press Esc, and a stroke moves and changes color like any drawing.

00:05:58.181 --> 00:06:01.665
Part 7. Ruler and drawing on indicators.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.936
The ruler is Alt+M or Shift+click.

00:06:04.986 --> 00:06:12.737
It shows the difference in price and percent, in ticks, bars and time, and in fractions of the daily ATR.

00:06:13.233 --> 00:06:17.253
Let’s add an indicator, with the button at the top or the slash key.

00:06:17.303 --> 00:06:19.408
We take the Relative Strength Index.

00:06:19.904 --> 00:06:27.901
You can draw in an indicator pane too: levels, lines and the ruler use the indicator values, and the magnet snaps to its line.

00:06:27.951 --> 00:06:31.861
For example, an overbought level on the RSI and a ruler on it.

00:06:32.312 --> 00:06:35.364
Part 8. Long and short positions.

00:06:37.351 --> 00:06:40.698
Long and short positions work like in TradingView.

00:06:40.748 --> 00:06:43.619
Pick the tool and click at the entry price.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:50.821
The stop is set automatically at 10% of the daily ATR, and the target by the R/R ratio, 5 to 1 by default.

00:06:51.318 --> 00:06:58.478
Entry, stop and target are dragged with the mouse and snap to candle prices; hold Shift to drag without the magnet.

00:06:58.528 --> 00:07:00.108
Or type them on the panel.

00:07:00.603 --> 00:07:05.420
The R/R field sets the ratio: change it to 3 and the target moves closer.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:10.954
With the lock on, stop and target are linked: drag the stop and the target follows.

00:07:11.459 --> 00:07:15.604
The chart shows how the trade is going, with the result in units of risk.

00:07:15.654 --> 00:07:20.488
And if you set a deposit and risk in the settings, the label shows the position size.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:25.040
Ctrl+C copies the position as text: entry, stop and target.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:33.276
And the other way round: paste such text and the position is rebuilt from it, or a new one appears if none is selected.

00:07:33.727 --> 00:07:36.515
Part 9. Quick paste and Share.

00:07:37.922 --> 00:07:45.864
The fastest way to open a setup is to paste a line from your notes or a spreadsheet: date, coin, direction and level.

00:07:45.914 --> 00:07:49.280
Copy the line and press Ctrl+V right on the chart.

00:07:49.776 --> 00:07:56.790
The terminal opens the coin, sets the direction and level, adds it to the current list and moves the charts to the date.

00:07:57.291 --> 00:08:03.099
You can paste several lines at once, and the coins go to the current list with directions and levels.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.361
There is also a “Paste as text” window.

00:08:05.856 --> 00:08:13.976
The Result column shows how far the price is from the nearest level in fractions of the daily ATR, or the result of a position if there is one.

00:08:14.477 --> 00:08:18.144
The Share button shows the nearest levels and latest positions.

00:08:18.194 --> 00:08:22.214
Tick what you need and get a link, a QR code or text for a messenger.

00:08:22.264 --> 00:08:25.282
For the recipient everything opens and draws itself.

00:08:25.732 --> 00:08:28.280
Part 10. Trade checklist.

00:08:29.091 --> 00:08:31.372
The checklist is its own tab, Alt+K.

00:08:31.422 --> 00:08:37.392
Tick the style, level type, conditions and entry, and a note appears on the chart right away.

00:08:37.442 --> 00:08:39.464
Answers are remembered per coin.

00:08:39.959 --> 00:08:45.624
The checklist text can be copied, and the “on chart” box decides whether the note is shown.

00:08:45.674 --> 00:08:49.517
The gear opens block setup: questions, answers and conditions.

00:08:49.967 --> 00:08:53.067
Part 11. ATR and indicators.

00:08:53.861 --> 00:09:02.281
The legend shows the daily ATR, the average of five previous daily candles, how much of it is used today and the stop size.

00:09:02.331 --> 00:09:09.443
The ATR table on lower intervals, with stop, target, slack and day bounds, is toggled by the ATR button.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:21.326
Indicators: volume, moving averages, Bollinger, VWAP, RSI, MACD, stochastic, ATR, and for futures the CDV volume delta and open interest.

00:09:21.376 --> 00:09:26.001
Parameters and colors are changed right from the legend.

00:09:26.451 --> 00:09:28.927
Part 12. Price alerts.

00:09:29.724 --> 00:09:33.132
Set an alert with a right-click on the chart or with Alt+A.

00:09:33.182 --> 00:09:37.001
Its line can be grabbed with the mouse and moved to another price.

00:09:37.513 --> 00:09:44.607
When the price reaches the level, the terminal shows a message and plays a sound, and unread alerts are counted on the bell.

00:09:44.657 --> 00:09:46.854
Alerts work while the terminal is open.

00:09:47.304 --> 00:09:50.164
Part 13. Watchlist dashboard.

00:09:50.978 --> 00:09:54.515
The dashboard opens with the toolbar button or Alt+D.

00:09:54.565 --> 00:10:01.215
At the top is a summary: coins and directions, trades, coins near a level, room to move and alerts.

00:10:01.265 --> 00:10:05.072
Below are the details, and clicking a row opens the coin.

00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:09.630
Part 14. Snapshots, settings and hotkeys.

00:10:10.457 --> 00:10:18.750
The camera saves all windows as one picture, and the button next to it copies the snapshot to the clipboard, ready to paste into a chat.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.695
The camera menu also has the active window only.

00:10:22.197 --> 00:10:28.157
Candle, background and grid colors are set separately for the light and dark themes.

00:10:28.207 --> 00:10:33.165
The interface language is switched in the settings, without reloading.

00:10:33.668 --> 00:10:37.073
All hotkeys are in the help, and search finds the one you need.

00:10:37.123 --> 00:10:43.106
Next to it are the Tutorial button with this overview and the heart, if you would like to support the project.

00:10:43.556 --> 00:10:46.104
Part 15. Device sync.

00:10:46.905 --> 00:10:49.022
Sync is turned on in the settings.

00:10:49.072 --> 00:10:56.414
Lists with directions, levels and drawings, alerts, the checklist and templates become the same on all your devices.

00:10:56.909 --> 00:10:59.882
A second device connects with the link or QR code.

00:10:59.932 --> 00:11:07.078
There is no server of our own: data is encrypted on the device and goes through public relays that only see ciphertext.

00:11:07.128 --> 00:11:10.283
The link is the key to your data, so keep it private.

00:11:10.734 --> 00:11:13.786
Part 16. The terminal on a phone.

00:11:14.604 --> 00:11:20.994
Open the sync link on your phone, and it has the same lists, levels, positions and alerts as the computer.

00:11:21.501 --> 00:11:28.923
The chart fills the screen, template windows switch with the tabs at the top, and the button next to them shows all windows at once.

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:36.244
Under the chart is a strip with neighbouring coins of the list: arrows or a swipe step through them without leaving the chart.

00:11:36.754 --> 00:11:41.699
At the bottom are the sections: screener, lists, checklist and alerts.

00:11:41.749 --> 00:11:43.768
Tap a coin to open its chart.

00:11:44.263 --> 00:11:46.337
The pencil opens the drawing tools.

00:11:46.387 --> 00:11:55.502
Paste works without a keyboard too: copy a trade or lines with coins and press the paste button in the list, in the More menu or on the position panel.

00:11:55.998 --> 00:12:01.728
Turn the phone sideways and navigation moves to a column on the left while the chart takes the full width.

00:12:01.778 --> 00:12:05.436
The terminal can be added to the home screen and starts like an app.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:06.477
That’s it.

00:12:06.527 --> 00:12:13.283
Start with the screener and watchlists, add your levels, turn on sync, and come back to the rest when you need it.

00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:14.119
Happy trading!
